Well, after innumerable tries, I have ascended a character.
Congratulations to Elvis the Samurai. Elvis was level 30 (392 HP), and
scored 7 555 038 points in 164 406 turns. Elvis died 4 times, including
once on the Astral plane.

Elvis was armed and dangerous, carrying the +4 ToM, +3 Excalibur, and +0
Demonbane (which he didn't use once). AC was rather poor -- only -7 by
the very end of the game, although it went as low as -21 for a while.

Game highlights: (some of this may be considered spoilers: proceed at
your own risk)


Probably the most annoying moment was when I was carrying a heavy corpse
to an altar for sacrifice, and some naga or other pops up out of nowhere
and disintegrates half my armor, including my GDSM, before I get a
chance to react. I eventually went through the game with +2 RDSM, which
I chucked in the very endgame for +0 GDSM, that I got through a lucky
wish. Enchant armor scrolls were extremely difficult to come by, and I
found only one magic marker. I had a lot of trouble with that pesky AoY
teleporting me back down levels in Gehnennom. Ooh, I hate when that
happens.

I killed the Wizard 12 times, Famine 3 times, and Death, as well as
Asmodeus, Orcus, Yeenoghu, and Orcus. Oh, a gremlin stole my cold
resistance on level 52, just after I had opened the entrance to Moloch's
sanctum.

Genocided: L's (liches, demiliches, master liches, lasagnas), ;'s (giant
eels, electric eels, and krakens), and mind flayers.

This is going to be a good spring break.
